P StarPath():
P   1. Create structure (array) to hold open set
P   2. Create structure (hashmap) to hold visited list
P   3. Call NearestNeighbor() to set origin
P   4. Update origin g_cost
P   5. Update origin path_cost
P     a. g_cost + CalculateEuclideanDistance()
P   6. Add origin to open set before passing to StarPathBuild()
P   7. Call  StarPathBuild()
P 
P StarPathBuild():
P   1. current_star = PopMin(open_set); 
P     a. Is current star the destination?
P       i. Yes? Reconstruct and return path using came_from pointers
P     b. Is current star already in visited list?
P       i. Skip
P      ii. Repeat from step 0
P   2. If curr star is not in visited list, add to visited list
P   3. Radius = distance(current, destination) * 0.5
P        repeat:
P          neighbors = GetNeighbors(root, current, radius)
P          if neighbors < 5: radius += 1
P        until neighbors >= 5
P   4. Find Euclidean distance to each neighbor and update
P     a. tentative_g_cost = g_cost + distance(current, neighbor)
P       i. If tentative_g_cost < neighbor->g_cost
P         1. Update neighbor's path_cost
P         2. Update neighbor->came_from to current star
P   5. Add each neighbor of current star to open set
P     a. Append each neighbor to end of heap
P     b. Call SiftUp() to correct heap violations
P   6. Loop back to step 0
